//? Title: Learned GeM descriptors and exact gallery retrieval
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Generalized-mean pooling learns how much to emphasize large feature activations. Hand derivatives and exact AP/ranking fixtures precede full descriptor checks,actual class-disjoint CIFAR images and visible hard-triplet Adam. Restored immutable deployment and every serialized gallery ranking are verified before showing actual nearest neighbors.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/image_retrieval.cpp`.

> The method

Encode observed RGB into unit descriptors with a learned GeM power,select hard triplets from frozen current embeddings,and recompute their hinge gradient for explicit Adam. Select checkpoints by exact validation mAP and compare held-out semantic retrieval with untrained and fixed pixel descriptors.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/image_retrieval_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/image_retrieval_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/image_retrieval_concept.tikz > build/image_retrieval_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/image_retrieval_concept.svg build/image_retrieval_concept.dvi > build/image_retrieval_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
