> Exact ranking,self exclusion and average precision

The index copies finite descriptors and computes squared differences in
Float64. It excludes a gallery item with the query’s source ID,then sorts
ascending distance,breaking exact ties by integer source ID. Identical,orthogonal
and opposite unit vectors have squared distances0,2,4. These exact small values
make ranking and self exclusion easy to audit.

For a query with R relevant eligible gallery items,noninterpolated average
precision is \(AP=R^{-1}\sum_{k:\,relevant(k)} P@k\). Relevant items at ranks1
and3 give \((1+2/3)/2=5/6\). Queries with no relevant gallery items after self
exclusion are counted separately and excluded from mean AP/hit rates. Rank
one and rank five hits ask whether any relevant item appears in that prefix.

Integer IDs remain integer throughout sorting and export. The native large-ID
regression uncovered and fixed a core `Tensor::to_vector`/`item` double
intermediate:IDs beyond2^53 now retain all bits,including strided views and
signed64-bit limits. The complete35-test tensor value suite passes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/image_retrieval_ranking.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto gallery = n::tensor({1., 0., 0., 1., -1., 0., 1., 0.}, {4, 2}),
             queries = n::tensor({1., 0., 1., 0.}, {2, 2});
  m::TensorDescriptorIndex index(gallery, {9, 3, 7, 2});
  const auto ranking = index.Rank(queries, 0, 9);
  const auto metrics = m::ScoreTensorRetrieval(queries, {1, 99}, {9, 90}, index, {1, 0, 1, 1});
  if (std::abs(metrics.map.item() - 5. / 6) > 1e-12 || metrics.eligible.item<int>() != 1 ||
      metrics.without_positive.item<int>() != 1)
    return 1;
  const auto ids = ranking.ids.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  const auto distance = ranking.distances.to_vector<double>();
  std::print("| rank | source ID | squared distance | relevant |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i)
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.0f} | {} |\n", i + 1, ids[i], distance[i], i != 1);
  const std::int64_t odd = 9007199254740993LL;
  m::TensorDescriptorIndex large(n::ones({2, 2}), {odd + 1, odd});
  const auto exact = large.Rank(n::ones({1, 2}), 0).ids.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  if (exact[0] != odd || exact[1] != odd + 1)
    return 1;
  std::print("Self ID9 excluded;AP5/6,eligible1,no-positive1. Exact large tied IDs {}/{} "
             "survive tensor export.\n",
             exact[0], exact[1]);
  auto a = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), b = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  a.bars({1, 2, 3}, distance, "squared distance", {37, 99, 235}, .6)
      .title("Self-excluded exact gallery ranking")
      .x_label("rank;IDs2,3,7")
      .y_label("squared descriptor distance")
      .y_limits(0, 5.2);
  b.lines({1, 2, 3}, {1, .5, 2. / 3}, "precision", {22, 163, 74})
      .points({1, 3}, {1, 2. / 3}, "relevant rank", {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Noninterpolated AP is5/6")
      .x_label("rank after self exclusion")
      .y_label("precision in ranked prefix")
      .y_limits(0, 1.3);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/image_retrieval_ranking.svg");
}
```
