> Actual CIFAR pools,disjoint classes and disjoint source images

Original CIFAR-10 binary records supply raw byte ingress. Only selected image
rows are converted:planar bytes enter an integer tensor before channel
transposition,Float32 conversion and division by255. A native independent
source-style loader verifies **every selected pixel,label and ID** exactly.
All row/category choices are metadata;std::mt19937(211) preserves the source
bucket-shuffle order within the same C++ standard library.

| Pool | Images | Original CIFAR categories | Images per category |
|---|---:|---|---:|
| Fitting |160|0–4|32|
| Validation queries/gallery |16/32|5–6|8/16|
| Test queries/gallery |48/96|7–9|16/32|

Every source ID is unique across all five pools. Official test IDs receive an
offset100000;development IDs retain their original row numbers. Relevance is
**same semantic category**,not a photograph of the same particular object.
This labelled CIFAR adaptation differs from the paper’s unlabelled3D-model
mining and particular-object benchmarks. The preview shows actual fitting
photographs,two per category0–4.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/image_retrieval_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
