\caption(Complete compact fitting with visible frozen hard mining,recomputed hinge and Adam. Separate panels show training hinge,validation mAP/hit1,and the small but actual learned GeM-power change. Validation mAP selects the restored checkpoint.)
\alttext(Complete compact fitting with visible frozen hard mining,recomputed hinge and Adam. Separate panels show training hinge,validation mAP/hit1,and the small but actual learned GeM-power change. Validation mAP selects the restored checkpoint.)

\image(figures/image_retrieval_baselines.svg)
\caption(Actual held-out exact retrieval comparisons. Models0–3 are learned CNN,untrained CNN,8x8 pooled RGB,and mean RGB. All use the same48 queries/96 gallery images and source-ID tie/self-exclusion rules.)
\alttext(Held-out mean AP and first-neighbor relevance for the learned descriptor and three simple references.)

\image(figures/image_retrieval_neighbors.png)
\caption(Eight actual held-out query rows in source order0,16,32,1,17,33,2,18. Each row is a blue-bordered query followed by its five exact nearest gallery neighbors. Green borders mark the same CIFAR category;red borders mark another category. No query labels enter descriptor inference.)
\alttext(Actual held-out horse,ship and truck queries with five ranked neighbors and semantic relevance borders.)

This small from-scratch semantic retrieval fit is deliberately bounded. Its
mAP,first-neighbor hits and pixel references can disagree about improvement.
The source protocol does not establish particular-object retrieval performance
or reproduce the paper’s training data,pretraining,whitening or benchmarks.

The selected epoch2 reaches held-out mAP.402486 versus.383918 for the
untrained CNN,but rank-one relevance drops from.375000 to.291667. Mean RGB
reaches mAP.434927 and rank-one relevance.479167. This short learned fit does
not outperform the fixed color reference. The printed metrics and actual
neighbor gallery show that limitation rather than implying a general CNN
retrieval advantage.

> Conclusion

Tensor image ingress,mining,ranking and AP preserve source sampling/tie rules while keeping the optimizer visible. Integer ID extraction now remains exact beyond double precision. Actual held-out neighbors and fixed color/pixel references expose this short semantic experiment’s limits without an instance-retrieval accuracy claim.

> References

- [Radenović,Tolias and Chum(2018),Fine-tuning CNN Image Retrieval with No Human Annotation](https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.02512).
- [Authors’ original GeM implementation](https://github.com/filipradenovic/cnnimageretrieval-pytorch/blob/master/cirtorch/layers/functional.py).
- [Krizhevsky,CIFAR-10 dataset and original binary layout](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html).
